Z||000000||dennis_6||10-21-2001||06:33 PM||||Where can I buy a fuel pressure gauge that hooks to the schrader valve.  I like the permanent version better, but the test type is fine too.  I just want a cheap one.  Thanks.<P>      ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Loki||10-21-2001||06:59 PM||||Check out the fiero store, they have one.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/loki_sig.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/w4[1].gif"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000002||dennis_6||10-21-2001||07:05 PM||||The Fiero store is way to high on theirs.<p>[This message has been edited by dennis_6 (edited 10-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||10-21-2001||11:30 PM||||Any auto parts store.  I got one from Pep Boys for about $45.  Screws onto the schrader valve on the fuel rail.  There are two different sizes for GM FI cars, so make sure you get one for your year and type of engine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||dennis_6||10-22-2001||05:37 AM||||Thanks Formula88!  Hillsboro does't have a pep boys, but almost everyone else.  Guess I will go shopping.  And thanks to everyone who responded.||||reg||1
Z||000005||chester||10-22-2001||07:21 AM||||Be sure to get a fluid filled gauge.  I got the one from the Fiero Store which A)was over priced and B)is not totally sealed so dust will get in the INSIDE of the gauge and make it look like hell in a short amount of time.  I got one made by Engine Works from my local speed shop that is oil filled and cost me $20.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000006||dennis_6||10-25-2001||10:23 PM||||Chester do they have a website.  Twenty dollars is the cheapest I have seen.||||reg||1
