Z||000015||grinthock||11-01-2001||07:45 PM||||Where is that shrayder valve and how do I get to it?  I wanna test my pressure.<P>Also what kind of Fuel/Air meter system do you have?  I Love it.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000016||grinthock||11-02-2001||06:52 AM||||bump ?||||reg||1
Z||000017||1FST2M6||11-02-2001||08:35 AM||||look at the coolant fill tube.. now look just to the drivers-side of it.. there is a small aluminum cap unscrew the cap and POOF open schrader valve if you don't have the right tool for it you'll have to take the actual valve out.. a small screw driver or schrader valve removal tool from walmart for $2 will do the trick. the air/fuel injector duty cycle monitor is made by hal tech and you can get one for about $100 plus shipping... takes about an hour to install.||||reg||1
